+/-
+wasm64 port: the syntax of the tactics both Knights and Knaves worlds teach
+(`knight_or_knave`, `knight_interp`, `knave_interp`), declared once.
+
+The DSL world (`dsl_KnightsAndKnaves`) and the set-theory world
+(`settheory_knightsknavesfoundation`) each declared these with `macro`, so each
+world had its own syntax with the same tokens. Upstream that is harmless: a
+level imports only its own world. The wasm64 build checks every level in one
+environment that holds the whole game. There the parser returns both syntaxes
+and Lean runs only the first one (a choice of syntaxes falls through only on
+unsupported syntax), so the DSL levels ran the set-theory expansions and
+failed. With one syntax here and each world's expansions as `macro_rules`,
+Lean tries the expansions in turn and keeps the first that succeeds, as it
+already does for the `contradiction` extensions both worlds add.
+-/
+
+/-- Case split on whether an islander is a knight or a knave. -/
+syntax "knight_or_knave" term "with" rcasesPat rcasesPat : tactic
+/-- Case split on whether an islander is a knight or a knave. -/
+syntax "knight_or_knave" term : tactic
+
+/-- Interpret statements in terms of knaves -/
+syntax "knave_interp" : tactic
+/-- Interpret statements in terms of knaves -/
+syntax "knave_interp" "at" Lean.Parser.Tactic.locationHyp : tactic
+/-- Interpret statements in terms of knaves -/
+syntax "knave_interp" "at" Lean.Parser.Tactic.locationWildcard : tactic
+
+/-- Interpret statements in terms of knights -/
+syntax "knight_interp" : tactic
+/-- Interpret statements in terms of knights -/
+syntax "knight_interp" "at" Lean.Parser.Tactic.locationHyp : tactic
+/-- Interpret statements in terms of knights -/
+syntax "knight_interp" "at" Lean.Parser.Tactic.locationWildcard : tactic
